  "id": "lol_mod",
  "mod_id": "lol_mod",
  "name": "League Champions & Rift Quality Pack / \u82f1\u96c4\u4e0e\u5ce1\u8c37\u54c1\u8d28\u5347\u7ea7",
  "author": "BoDUD",
  "version": "0.10.16",
  "description": "Adds Shen and reworks official champions 002-007 and 009 as Lucian, Orianna, Briar, Sivir, Kled, Xayah and Yone. Version 0.10.16 targets Teamfight Manager 2 base 0.5.1 and uses the matching official 0.5.1 SDK. Versions 0.10.11 through 0.10.15 are retained as failed portrait-route records: 0.10.11 assumed dynamic card roots were named by champion id, 0.10.12 required an unreachable ChampionInfoUIRunner, 0.10.13 mistook screenshot pixels for RenderCommand geometry, 0.10.14 fixed only the separate 85x93 management-card route, and 0.10.15 assumed the BP source command itself was 90x122. Its live telemetry instead proved the visible central BP actor is a Yone NinePatch in the UI pass at 95x88, while the same texture's Sprite command is in the Game pass. The default 0.10.16 Yone-only extension therefore matches only the measured UI NinePatch source geometry with a narrow rounding allowance, replaces it with the source-direct ui/champion_portrait/dual_blader_grid texture, restores the texture's natural 90x122 output geometry, preserves horizontal center and top y, clears the texture rectangle and borders, and enables nearest sampling. Its visible alpha ends at source y=85, so the full legs and boots remain inside the BP icon's 88px region while the lower canvas is transparent. The 85x93 management, compact and scoreboard routes remain independent; Game-pass RenderCommand::Sprite battle actors, picked-side cards and other champions cannot match. The broader legacy MatchUIRunner, ClientDatabase, picked-side splash, dragon, server and other-champion rewrites remain explicitly opt-in. Bounded telemetry records the actual Yone command variant, pass, source and output geometry plus a dedicated yone_bp_grid_replace event. V6 keeps the official 3502x88 battle canvas, 13 animation tags, rectangles, labels and timings; Q/W/R gameplay, effects, icons and audio remain unchanged, as does the saved-season floor introduced in 0.10.5. A save first created on 0.10.5 or later remains valid. Spirit Cleave still performs one stateless 80-degree, 42000-range GameCtx cone scan with no process-global ledger, deals 35 + 45% Attack + 6% target maximum-health physical damage, and settles one shield tier for zero through five champions hit; Mod API 0.8 still requires fixed 0.5-second cast and 8-second cooldown. Retired E and 0.10.4 rectangular-W native names remain no-op saved-data compatibility only so old embedded trees do not crash after BP. Automated source and build checks do not constitute live visual acceptance; the 0.10.16 route remains pending in-game user verification.",
  "last_updated": "2026-07-21",
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "mod_id": "base",
      "version": ">=0.5.1"
    }
  ]
}
